(5576912, 804836, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: Not familiar with the song itself, but the sunset shot says enough.  Hard to get a fix on it in terms of place, doesn''t look like a big-city skyline.<br/> <br/>Technical: Good use of ambient light, a little glare from sun, use of thirds good with the low horizon. Like the underlit cloud on the right.<br/> <br/>Artistic: I like the boats'' silhouettes on the water, help add interest and depth to the shot.<br/> <br/>Overall: Would have liked to see this with a slightly faster aperture, like 1/40 or 1/50.<br/> <br/>Feel free to pm me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: Not familiar with the song itself, but the sunset shot says enough.  Hard to get a fix on it in terms of place, doesn''t look like a big-city skyline. Technical: Good use of ambient light, a little glare from sun, use of thirds good with the low horizon. Like the underlit cloud on the right. Artistic: I like the boats'' silhouettes on the water, help add interest and depth to the shot. Overall: Would have liked to see this with a slightly faster aperture, like 1/40 or 1/50. Feel free to pm me with any questions, Susan', '2009-07-16 20:58:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5576926, 804365, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: This shot''s underlying sadness and poignancy surprises me.  I used to have several friends in the drag community and yes, many of them did indeed feel lost without a drag/cross-dressing persona to complete them.<br/> <br/>Technical: Composition interesting, lighting good, no glare or harsh shadows.  Might have liked to see a little bit of light bounced up into the side of your made-up face to emphasize the difference.  I personally like the slightly oof reflection, but dpc leans toward tack-sharp focus.<br/> <br/>Artistic: At the risk of sounding corny, very reflective.  Would have been too easy to make direct eye contact with your reflection.  The 3/4 profile visible in mirror adds interest.  Good contrast between the macho cowboy look and the made-up drag queen. And I like the flower on the mirror, it''s a feminine icon and helps draw attention up to the female side.<br/> <br/>Overall: As I said before, I sense a melancholiness here, and that coupled with the makeup probably made more conservative voters uneasy and hence cast lower votes.  This community does favour the very obvious.<br/> <br/>FWIW: Should you choose to do cross-dressing again, don''t stint on the makeup!  Drag queens do it to get noticed, so they go all out and slap on the rouge, bright lips, eyeshadow etc.<br/> <br/>Feel free to pm me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: This shot''s underlying sadness and poignancy surprises me.  I used to have several friends in the drag community and yes, many of them did indeed feel lost without a drag/cross-dressing persona to complete them. Technical: Composition interesting, lighting good, no glare or harsh shadows.  Might have liked to see a little bit of light bounced up into the side of your made-up face to emphasize the difference.  I personally like the slightly oof reflection, but dpc leans toward tack-sharp focus. Artistic: At the risk of sounding corny, very reflective.  Would have been too easy to make direct eye contact with your reflection.  The 3/4 profile visible in mirror adds interest.  Good contrast between the macho cowboy look and the made-up drag queen. And I like the flower on the mirror, it''s a feminine icon and helps draw attention up to the female side. Overall: As I said before, I sense a melancholiness here, and that coupled with the makeup probably made more conservative voters uneasy and hence cast lower votes.  This community does favour the very obvious. FWIW: Should you choose to do cross-dressing again, don''t stint on the makeup!  Drag queens do it to get noticed, so they go all out and slap on the rouge, bright lips, eyeshadow etc. Feel free to pm me with any questions, Susan', '2009-07-16 21:15:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(5577187, 804829, 31637, '<td valign="top">Hello, found this in the critique club section:<br/> <br/>My first thought is if it fits the challenge, and it does give that the window for this challenge was wide open. The technicality of the shot looks very orthodox for a horizontal landscape, well done filling the bottom half of the frame with all the land and giving just enough colorful sky on the top. I love the rule of 3rds used for the sun and the positioning of the logs.<br/> <br/>Color wise, very conservative and satisfying. However, it could be a bit more vivid. The DOF could use improvement. I don''t mind the flare coming from the sun, the aperture seems perfect for the sunset shot, but that shutter speed is way high! Maybe too high, good choice leaving the ISO at 100 though. <br/> <br/>Great landscape, very above average, I voted this a 6 during voting btw.<br/></td>', 'Hello, found this in the critique club section: My first thought is if it fits the challenge, and it does give that the window for this challenge was wide open. The technicality of the shot looks very orthodox for a horizontal landscape, well done filling the bottom half of the frame with all the land and giving just enough colorful sky on the top. I love the rule of 3rds used for the sun and the positioning of the logs. Color wise, very conservative and satisfying. However, it could be a bit more vivid. The DOF could use improvement. I don''t mind the flare coming from the sun, the aperture seems perfect for the sunset shot, but that shutter speed is way high! Maybe too high, good choice leaving the ISO at 100 though.  Great landscape, very above average, I voted this a 6 during voting btw.', '2009-07-17 00:57:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(5577219, 804841, 31637, '<td valign="top">Hello, found this in a Critique Club section: <br/> <br/>Since the challenge was wide open, this photograph does fit it if the title of the image is in fact part of a Micheal Jackson song. The subject seems much more powerful than 2000 Watts though...I am just speculating. <br/> <br/>The image itself is awesome, I REALLY love the blue sky, and the vantage point is great. Its rare to see such timely captures of lighting like this, and the way it lit up the sky makes this for me. <br/> <br/>But as for the bolt, nothing too fascinating about the geology. It''s a group of high plains, fit into the frame well. I think this is underrated, since I scored it a 6 during voting.<br/></td>', 'Hello, found this in a Critique Club section:  Since the challenge was wide open, this photograph does fit it if the title of the image is in fact part of a Micheal Jackson song. The subject seems much more powerful than 2000 Watts though...I am just speculating.  The image itself is awesome, I REALLY love the blue sky, and the vantage point is great. Its rare to see such timely captures of lighting like this, and the way it lit up the sky makes this for me.  But as for the bolt, nothing too fascinating about the geology. It''s a group of high plains, fit into the frame well. I think this is underrated, since I scored it a 6 during voting.', '2009-07-17 02:18:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(5578258, 803228, 31637, '<td valign="top">The photo is a real masterpiece, could easily have won; I think the model looks like Slash more than MJ! Or isn''t that how he looked when he played the scarecrow in the Oz remake? Nice job.</td>', 'The photo is a real masterpiece, could easily have won; I think the model looks like Slash more than MJ! Or isn''t that how he looked when he played the scarecrow in the Oz remake? Nice job.', '2009-07-18 06:41:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5578263, 804590, 31637, '<td valign="top">Hello, found this in the Critique Club section:<br/> <br/>I think the photo fits the challenge of course, but maybe another title would fit the photo more. Its not the most important thing however. I love the composition, how the bloom of light fills up the whole frame. Color seems ok, maybe a bit white in areas. The Flaws are the whites, especially on the water. Maybe 3 seconds or less might have worked for the exposure. <br/> <br/>Overall, I still think its underrated, fireworks are not easy to shoot.</td>', 'Hello, found this in the Critique Club section: I think the photo fits the challenge of course, but maybe another title would fit the photo more. Its not the most important thing however. I love the composition, how the bloom of light fills up the whole frame. Color seems ok, maybe a bit white in areas. The Flaws are the whites, especially on the water. Maybe 3 seconds or less might have worked for the exposure.  Overall, I still think its underrated, fireworks are not easy to shoot.', '2009-07-18 06:53:05.000000', NULL, 0),
